    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="12">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IVEg">IV Eg</ref> 12</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="12" corresp="#wit-f"><pb n="212" ed="#liebermann"/>Þonne wille ic, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> stande mid Denum swa gode laga swa hy betste geceosen, ⁊ ic heom á geþafode ⁊ geþafian wille, swa lange swa me lif gelæst, for eowrum hyldum, þe ge me symble cyddon.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="12" corresp="#wit-c"><pb n="212" ed="#liebermann"/>Þonne wille ic, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> stande mid Denu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> swa gode laga swa hy betste<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IVEg_12.lnote.oe.3"/> geceosen, ⁊ ic heom á geþafode ⁊ geðafian wille, swa lange swa me lif gelæst, for eowrum hyldum, þe ge me symble cyddon.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="12" corresp="#wit-c"><pb n="36" ed="#robertson"/>Þonne wille ic þæt stande mid Denum swa gode laga swa hy betste geceosen; ⁊ ic heom á geþafode ⁊ geðafian wille, swa lange swa me lif gelæst, for eowrum hyldum þe ge me symble cyddon.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IVEg_12.lnote.de.1"/><pb n="213" ed="#liebermann"/>Ferner will ich, dass bei den Dänen [Nordleuten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IVEg_12.lnote.de.2"/>] so gute Verfassung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IVEg_12.lnote.de.3"/> bestehe, wie sie als beste erwählen wollen und ich ihnen stets verstattet habe und verstatten werde, so<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IVEg_12.lnote.de.4"/> lange als mir das Leben bleibt, wegen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IVEg_12.lnote.de.5"/> eurer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IVEg_12.lnote.de.6"/> Treue<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IVEg_12.lnote.de.7"/>, die ihr mir stets bekundet habt.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Further I will that among the Danes [Northmen] there stand as good laws as they choose as best, and as I have always allowed them and will allow them as long as my life lasts, because of your loyalty, which you have always shown me.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-c"><pb n="37" ed="#robertson"/>Further, it is my will that the Danes continue to observe the best constitution which they can determine upon<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IVEg_12.robnote.n.1"/>. I<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IVEg_12.robnote.n.2"/> have always granted you such a concession and will continue to do so, as long as my life lasts, because of the loyalty<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IVEg_12.robnote.n.3"/> which you have constantly professed to me.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IVEg_12.whinote.n.2"/><pb n="440" ed="#whitelock"/>Further, it is my will that there should be in force among the Danes such good laws as they best decide on, and I have ever allowed them this and will allow it as long as my life lasts, because of your loyalty, which you have always shown me.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="213"><ref target="clause:IVEg_2-1">IV Eg 2.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. 2, 1</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="370"><label>shared word</label> <ref target="clause:Forf_3">Forf 3</ref> <quote>Particularly striking is 'standan' meaning 'to be valid [law]', Forf. 3, II Atr 9, with IV Eg 1:6, 2, 2:1–1a, 12, 15</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Not in the Latin Versio (12 and 12.1 are missing there). Liebermann compares IV Eg 2.1.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IVEg_12.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">212</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">letztes</hi> e <hi rend="italic">ausradirt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">last e erased</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVEg_12.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">143</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Versio lässt den Satz wie 14, 1 fort, weil sie nicht in Denalagu schreibt; <hi rend="italic">s. o</hi>. 6³</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The Versio omits the sentence, as at 14, 1, because it is not writing in the Denalagu; see above 6³</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVEg_12.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">143</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o</hi>. 2, 1³·⁴. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Dänen 12f.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">See above 2, 1³·⁴. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Dänen 12f.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVEg_12.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">143</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o</hi>. 2, 1³·⁴. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Dänen 12f.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">See above 2, 1³·⁴. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Dänen 12f.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVEg_12.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">143</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o</hi>. 2a⁵; <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 16</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">See above 2a⁵; <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 16</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVEg_12.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">143</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ebenso <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 14, 1. 16</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Likewise <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 14, 1. 16</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVEg_12.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">143</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o</hi>. 5²</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">See above 5²</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVEg_12.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">143</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Huld’ steht Agsä. öfter im Plural: <hi rend="italic">ic wæs on fullum hyldum hold</hi>; Testament XI. Jhs., Thorpe <hi rend="italic">Diplom</hi>. 508; <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. im <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi> trenne man hiervon <hi rend="italic">helde</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘Huld’ often stands in the plural in A.-S.: <hi rend="italic">ic wæs on fullum hyldum hold</hi>; will of the 11th cent., Thorpe <hi rend="italic">Diplom</hi>. 508; <hi rend="italic">above</hi> in the <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi>, <hi rend="italic">helde</hi> should be separated from this</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IVEg_12.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">309</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. cap. 2, 1.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IVEg_12.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">309</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">For similar changes of person see II Edm. Pre. and note.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IVEg_12.robnote.n.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">309</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">For the use of <hi rend="italic">hyld</hi> elsewhere in the plural see BT. p. 581, <hi rend="italic">s.v.</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IVEg_12.whinote.n.2" n="2" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">440</biblScope></bibl><label>12</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">id. omits these chapters</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
